# Reproducible PDFer style previews and validation gallery.
# PDFer's RASTER ORNAMENT CACHE - regenerated on demand, never source.
# pdfer_ornament.py writes these and the filename IS the cache key:
#   orn_<pattern>_<width>x<height>_<colour>_<seedhash>.png
# so every new palette, size or seed mints a new file and git nags forever.
# 15 of them were committed by accident with the PDFer styles work and were
# untracked on 2026-09-20 (kept on disk - it is a cache, not a deliverable).
# Nothing references them: not build.py, not copy_source_assets.py, not the
# tests, not scripts/verify_pdfer_styles.py.
Tlamatini/agent/agents/pdfer/_art/

/artifacts/pdfer-styles/
/output/pdf/pdfer-style-atlas.pdf

# Regenerable PPTXer verification decks, renders, galleries, and reports.
/artifacts/pptxer-visibility/
/artifacts/pptxer-styles/

# Reproducible LaTeXer style PDFs, rendered previews and QA report.
/artifacts/latexer-styles/
/output/pdf/latexer-style-atlas.pdf

# ⚠️ ESP32TemplateProject ships a `lib/README.md` documenting PlatformIO's
# private-library convention, and the generic Python-packaging rule `lib/` near
# the top of this file would silently swallow it — the template would reach every
# clone, every build and every user MISSING a directory its own README describes.
# These negations are deliberately narrow: they re-include ONLY that one template
# path, leaving the blanket `lib/` rule intact everywhere else. Git cannot
# re-include a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so the directory is un-ignored
# first and its contents second — both lines are required.
!Tlamatini/agent/agents/esp32er/ESP32TemplateProject/lib/
!Tlamatini/agent/agents/esp32er/ESP32TemplateProject/lib/**
